# update: the update line on top (a newer gtty on GitHub) and gtty ▸ Check
# for Updates….
# Run: zig build && GTTY_UPDATE_REPLY=test/update-reply.json \
#   GTTY_UPDATE_VERSION=0.2.1 GTTY_UPDATE_INSTALLER=apt GTTY_SHOW_DRY=1 \
#   zig-out/bin/gtty --script test/update.gt
# Expect: update-1: the yellow line "Newer version available: 0.4.0. Your
# version is 0.2.1." with the apt command's button; update-2: the button
# flashed, "copied the install command" (the clipboard has it); update-3:
# "would open https://github.com/gttyterm/gtty/releases/tag/v0.4.0";
# update-4: the line closed (×), the window back to the top; update-5:
# the menu's check brought it back, "gtty 0.4.0 is available".
s
/wait 1500
/shot update-1.bmp
/click 600 13
/wait 100
/shot update-2.bmp
/click 100 13
/wait 300
/shot update-3.bmp
/click 1083 13
/wait 600
/shot update-4.bmp
/menu check-updates
/wait 600
/shot update-5.bmp
/quit
